@node Examples
@chapter Examples

@cindex examples
The programs in @file{examples/} each have a @file{README.md}.  Run them
from the repository root:

@table @file
@item examples/compute/compute.scm
A headless compute shader that squares 1000 floats, using the raw API.

@item examples/gears/gears.scm
The classic spinning gears in an X11 window, with dynamic rendering.

@item examples/cube/cube.scm
A spinning, lit, textured cube in a native Wayland window, using only
libwayland-client.

@item examples/spirals/spirals.scm
A small neural network trained on the GPU with @code{(vulkan compute)}
to tell three interleaved spirals apart.
@end table

For example:

@example
guile -L . examples/spirals/spirals.scm
@end example

The tests are in @file{tests/}: @file{tests/compute.scm} checks every
@code{(vulkan compute)} operation against plain Guile, and
@file{tests/xcb-surface.scm} and @file{tests/wayland-presentation.scm}
check the window-system modules, and
@file{tests/compare-with-chez-vulkan.scm} checks that the bindings
match chez-vulkan's.  The continuous integration runs all of them, and
the examples, on Mesa's software Vulkan driver.

