@node Regenerating
@chapter Regenerating the Bindings

@cindex CastXML
@cindex generator
@file{vulkan.scm} and @file{vulkan/@{xlib,xcb,wayland@}.scm} are
generated by @file{generate.scm} from a
@uref{https://github.com/CastXML/CastXML, CastXML} parse of the Vulkan
headers, which needs the X11, Xrandr, XCB and Wayland development headers:

@example
castxml --castxml-gccxml -DVK_USE_PLATFORM_XLIB_KHR \
  -DVK_USE_PLATFORM_XLIB_XRANDR_EXT -DVK_USE_PLATFORM_XCB_KHR \
  -DVK_USE_PLATFORM_WAYLAND_KHR -o res/vulkan.xml /usr/include/vulkan/vulkan.h
guile generate.scm
@end example

@file{vulkan/win32.scm} comes from a second parse for 64-bit Windows,
which needs the Windows SDK and MSVC headers (for example from
msvc-wine).  The generator checks that the core module from that parse
is identical to @file{vulkan.scm}:

@example
WINSDK_INCLUDE=@dots{} MSVC_INCLUDE=@dots{} res/make-win32-xml.sh
guile generate.scm res/vulkan-win32.xml
@end example

Which functions get plain names is decided from the header section each
one is declared in, not from the installed loader, so regenerating
anywhere gives the same bindings.

